      W1-R 't Hooft modulus ratio (2.55e-12) is in a DIFFERENT
      channel (vertex / bare dS/dtau); the two are not numerically
      comparable but the hierarchy is:
          inverse-coupling shift  >>  modulus-vertex contribution
          6.278e-04 vs W1-R 2.55e-12   (ratio 2.46e+08x)
      Consistency: the inverse-coupling shift is larger than the
      modulus-vertex contribution because the modulus form carries an
      additional 1/Lambda^4 suppression and a smaller determinantal
      prefactor.  Both channels agree on the exponential exp(-S_inst),
      differing only by O(1) prefactors and phase-space dressings.
  (c) Dimensional analysis: [(c/2pi) exp(-S_inst)] = dimensionless (PASS)
  (d) Downward propagation: the instanton shift is UV-boundary,
      so Delta(1/alpha_s) is preserved under RGE running.  At M_Z,
      the same Delta shifts 1/alpha_s(M_Z) by the same amount,
      giving a fractional shift of 7.408e-05 at M_Z.
